---
description: MCP Watchdog repo conventions
alwaysApply: true
---
- VS Code extension, TypeScript strict. Bundle with esbuild (npm run build); typecheck is
  tsc --noEmit (npm run compile). Both must pass before you claim done.
- Only runtime dependency is @modelcontextprotocol/sdk. Do not add runtime deps without asking.
  devDependencies for testing/linting are fine.
- monitor.ts and config-core.ts (after task W1) must stay importable without the vscode module.
  All vscode API usage belongs in extension.ts, statusBar.ts, serversTree.ts, overviewView.ts,
  logger.ts, or thin glue.
- Never log or render values of server env vars or HTTP headers. Names are fine, values never.
- States are exactly: connecting | healthy | degraded | failed | disconnected. Do not add states
  without updating ui/statePresentation.ts, statusBar.ts, serversTree.ts, overviewView.ts together.
- Every new setting goes in package.json contributes.configuration with a default and description,
  and is read via vscode.workspace.getConfiguration('mcpWatchdog').
- Unit tests: vitest, in test/unit/, run with npm run test:unit. They must pass with no network
  and no VS Code host. Anything needing npx/network goes in scripts/ (smoke/integration tier).
- Update CHANGELOG.md (Keep a Changelog format) and README for any user-visible change.
- Do not bump version; the maintainer does releases.
- Do not add Co-authored-by trailers to commits. Never commit *.local.md or *.vsix.
